"Editors in the Agent Panel—such as the main message textarea—use monospace "
"fonts and are controlled by `agent_buffer_font_size` (which defaults to "
"`buffer_font_size` when unset)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:152
msgid "Default Tool Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:154
msgid ""
"**Note:** In Zed v0.224.0 and above, tool approval uses the `agent."
"tool_permissions` settings described below."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:156
msgid ""
"The `agent.tool_permissions.default` setting controls the baseline tool "
"approval behavior for Zed's native agent:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:158
msgid ""
"`\"confirm\"` (default) — Prompts for approval before running any tool action"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:159
msgid "`\"allow\"` — Auto-approves tool actions without prompting"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:160
msgid "`\"deny\"` — Blocks all tool actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:165 src/ai/agent-settings.md:188
#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:230 src/ai/agent-settings.md:257
msgid "\"tool_permissions\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:166 src/ai/agent-settings.md:189
#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:192 src/ai/agent-settings.md:260
#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:263
msgid "\"default\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:166 src/ai/agent-settings.md:192
#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:260
msgid "\"confirm\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:172
msgid ""
"Even with `\"default\": \"allow\"`, per-tool `always_deny` and "
"`always_confirm` patterns are still respected, so you can auto-approve most "
"actions while keeping guardrails on dangerous or sensitive ones."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:174
msgid "Per-tool Permission Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:176
msgid ""
"For granular control over individual tool actions, use the `tools` key "
"inside `tool_permissions` to configure regex-based rules that auto-approve, "
"auto-deny, or always require confirmation for specific inputs."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:178
msgid "Each tool entry supports the following keys:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:180
msgid ""
"`default` — Fallback when no patterns match: `\"confirm\"`, `\"allow\"`, or "
"`\"deny\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:181
msgid "`always_allow` — Array of patterns that auto-approve matching actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:182
msgid ""
"`always_deny` — Array of patterns that block matching actions immediately"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:183
msgid ""
"`always_confirm` — Array of patterns that always prompt for confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:189
msgid "\"allow\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:190 src/ai/agent-settings.md:231
#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:258
msgid "\"tools\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:191
msgid "\"terminal\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:193
msgid "\"always_allow\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:194 src/ai/agent-settings.md:195
#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:197 src/ai/agent-settings.md:198
#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:202 src/ai/agent-settings.md:203
#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:235
msgid "\"pattern\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:194
msgid "\"^cargo\\\\s+(build|test|check)\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:195
msgid "\"^git\\\\s+(status|log|diff)\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:197 src/ai/agent-settings.md:201
#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:233
msgid "\"always_deny\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:197
msgid "\"rm\\\\s+-rf\\\\s+(/|~)\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:198
msgid "\"always_confirm\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:198
msgid "\"sudo\\\\s\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:200 src/ai/agent-settings.md:232
msgid "\"edit_file\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:202
msgid "\"\\\\.env\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:203
msgid "\"\\\\.(pem|key)$\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:212
msgid "Pattern Precedence"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:214
msgid ""
"When evaluating a tool action, rules are checked in the following order "
"(highest priority first):"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:216
msgid ""
"**Built-in security rules** — Hardcoded protections (e.g., `rm -rf /`) that "
"cannot be overridden"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:217
msgid "**`always_deny`** — Blocks matching actions immediately"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:218
msgid "**`always_confirm`** — Requires confirmation for matching actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:219
msgid ""
"**`always_allow`** — Auto-approves matching actions. For the terminal tool "
"with chained commands (e.g., `echo hello && rm file`), **all** sub-commands "
"must match an `always_allow` pattern"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:220
msgid ""
"**Tool-specific `default`** — Per-tool fallback when no patterns match (e."
"g., `tools.terminal.default`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:221
msgid "**Global `default`** — Falls back to `tool_permissions.default`"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:223
msgid "Case Sensitivity"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:225
msgid ""
"Patterns are **case-insensitive** by default. To make a pattern case-"
"sensitive, set `case_sensitive` to `true`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:235
msgid "\"^Makefile$\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:236
msgid "\"case_sensitive\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:246
msgid "`copy_path` and `move_path` Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:248
msgid ""
"For the `copy_path` and `move_path` tools, patterns are matched "
"independently against both the source and destination paths. A `deny` or "
"`confirm` match on **either** path takes effect. For `always_allow`, "
"**both** paths must match for auto-approval."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:250
msgid "MCP Tool Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:252
msgid ""
"MCP tools use the key format `mcp:<server_name>:<tool_name>` in the `tools` "
"configuration. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:259
msgid "\"mcp:github:create_issue\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:262
msgid "\"mcp:github:create_pull_request\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:263
msgid "\"deny\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:271
msgid ""
"The `default` key on each MCP tool entry is the primary mechanism for "
"controlling MCP tool permissions. Pattern-based rules (`always_allow`, "
"`always_deny`, `always_confirm`) match against an empty string for MCP "
"tools, so most patterns won't match — use the tool-level `default` instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:273
msgid ""
"See the [Tool Permissions](./tool-permissions.md) documentation for more "
"examples and complete details."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:275
msgid ""
"**Note:** Before Zed v0.224.0, tool approval was controlled by the `agent."
"always_allow_tool_actions` boolean (default `false`). Set it to `true` to "
"auto-approve tool actions, or leave it `false` to require confirmation for "
"edits and tool calls."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:277
msgid "Edit Display Mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:279
msgid ""
"Control whether to display review actions (accept & reject) in single "
"buffers after the agent is done performing edits. The default value is "
"`false`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:285
msgid "\"single_file_review\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:290
msgid "Sound Notification"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:292
msgid ""
"Control whether to hear a notification sound when the agent is done "
"generating changes or needs your input. The default value is `never`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:294
msgid "`\"never\"` (default) — Never play the sound."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:295
msgid ""
"`\"when_hidden\"` — Only play the sound when the agent panel is not visible."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:296
msgid "`\"always\"` — Always play the sound on completion."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:301
msgid "\"play_sound_when_agent_done\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:301
msgid "\"never\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:306
msgid "Message Editor Size"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:308
msgid ""
"Use the `message_editor_min_lines` setting to control the minimum number of "
"lines of height the agent message editor should have. It is set to `4` by "
"default, and the max number of lines is always double of the minimum."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:314
msgid "\"message_editor_min_lines\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:319
msgid "Modifier to Send"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:321
msgid ""
"Require a modifier (`cmd` on macOS, `ctrl` on Linux) to send messages. "
"Prevents accidental sends while editing. The default value is `false`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:327
msgid "\"use_modifier_to_send\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:332
msgid "Edit Card"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:334
msgid ""
"Use the `expand_edit_card` setting to control whether edit cards show the "
"full diff in the Agent Panel. It is set to `true` by default, but if set to "
"false, the card's height is capped to a certain number of lines, requiring a "
"click to be expanded."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:340
msgid "\"expand_edit_card\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:345
msgid "Terminal Card"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:347
msgid ""
"Use the `expand_terminal_card` setting to control whether terminal cards "
"show the command output in the Agent Panel. It is set to `true` by default, "
"but if set to false, the card will be fully collapsed even while the command "
"is running, requiring a click to be expanded."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:353
msgid "\"expand_terminal_card\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:358
msgid "Feedback Controls"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:360
msgid ""
"Control whether to display the thumbs up/down buttons at the bottom of each "
"agent response, allowing you to give Zed feedback about the agent's "
"performance. The default value is `true`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-settings.md:366
msgid "\"enable_feedback\""
msgstr ""
